./data/living_catalog/taxonomy_rerun_preflight_2026-08-12/taxonomy/runs/classification_dense/shard_04/records/june_update_2026-06-10__rec_000121_8f4709456aba/june_update_2026_06_10_rec_000121_8f4709456aba_docling_json_20260812_214234/debug/dense_provenance.json:253:      "text": "RVQ-Alpha: Bridging Single-Cell Transcriptomics and Large Language Models via Discrete Tokenization and Verifiable Reinforcement Learning\nAbstract\nIntegrating continuous single-cell gene expression profiles with discrete-token large language models (LLMs) remains an open challenge: text-based methods are token-inefficient and discard quantitative precision, continuous embeddings preclude autoregressive generation, and single-codebook vector quantization cannot stratify biological scales.\nWe present RVQ-Alpha , an end-to-end framework that bridges this modality gap through three contributions:\n(i) a Residual Vector Quantization (RVQ) tokenizer that compresses each cell into a fixed 10-token sequence via eight residual codebooks embedded directly in the LLM vocabulary, requiring 3.4 \u00d7 fewer tokens than prior discrete methods and enabling bidirectional unification of cell interpretation and generation;\n(ii) scCoT-Synth , a teacher-student engine that grounds newly added biological tokens through evidence-before-conclusion reasoning, using the language modeling objective as the cross-modal alignment signal without a separate projection network;\nand (iii) a Fact-Aware RLVR system combining an ontology-grounded answer judge with saliency-weighted verification of biological claims against actual expression data, under dynamic gating that conditions hallucination suppression on task competence.\nBuilt on Qwen3-4B and trained via continued pretraining, supervised fine-tuning, and reinforcement learning, RVQ-Alpha substantially improves out-of-distribution generalization and rare-cell recognition across eight held-out datasets; ablations confirm that evidence-first grounding reduces hallucination more than fivefold.\n\u2217 \u2020 Equal contribution; \u2217 Corresponding authors: \u27e8 kongjiaming@renaissance-era.com \u27e9 , \u27e8 tian_luyi@gzlab.ac.cn \u27e9\navailable under a CC-BY-NC-ND 4.0 International license. (which was not certified by peer review) is the author/funder, who has granted bioRxiv a license to display the preprint in perpetuity. It is made bioRxiv preprint doi: https://doi.org/10.64898/2026.04.20.719773; this version posted April 23, 2026. The copyright holder for this preprint\nRVQ-Alpha: Bridging Single-Cell Transcriptomics and Large Language Models via Discrete Tokenization and Verifiable Reinforcement Learning",
./data/living_catalog/taxonomy_rerun_preflight_2026-08-12/taxonomy/runs/classification_dense/shard_04/records/june_update_2026-06-10__rec_000121_8f4709456aba/june_update_2026_06_10_rec_000121_8f4709456aba_docling_json_20260812_214234/debug/dense_provenance.json:669:      "text": "1 Introduction\n- We introduce RVQ discrete tokenization for single-cell transcriptomics, marking the first application of residual vector quantization to gene expression data. An eight-codebook residual quantizer (with 32 entries each) produces a representation of 10 tokens per cell embedded natively in the LLM vocabulary (\u00a73.2), requiring 60% fewer tokens than text-based approaches (Table 8). Furthermore, empirical analysis (\u00a76) demonstrates that earlier codebooks predominantly encode broader identity levels, whereas later codebooks refine within-lineage variation.\n- We develop scCoT-Synth , an evidence-grounded supervision engine that overcomes the coldstart problem of newly added biological tokens without requiring a cross-modal projector. By coupling constraint-conditioned rationale synthesis with a seven-layer verification stack, this engine aligns discrete token representations with gene-level semantics entirely through the language modeling loss.\n- We construct a multi-component RLVR reward system with Fact Verification that validates biological claims against actual expression data. This approach addresses the hallucination problem inherent in LLM-native biological tokenization, yielding up to a 4.6 \u00d7 improvement on population-level tasks (Table 9).",
./data/living_catalog/taxonomy_rerun_preflight_2026-08-12/taxonomy/runs/classification_dense/shard_04/records/june_update_2026-06-10__rec_000121_8f4709456aba/june_update_2026_06_10_rec_000121_8f4709456aba_docling_json_20260812_214234/debug/dense_provenance.json:1601:      "text": "3 Method\nRVQ-Alpha integrates four components into an end-to-end framework for single-cell transcriptomic reasoning: (i) a residual-quantization cell tokenizer that embeds gene expression into the native token vocabulary of the LLM (\u00a73.2), (ii) a scCoT-Synth pipeline that constructs evidence-first chain-of-thought training data (\u00a73.3), (iii) a three-stage training pipeline progressing from token grounding through multi-task SFT to reinforcement learning (\u00a73.4), and (iv) a multi-teacher distillation and fact-aware reward system that unifies multi-task capabilities while suppressing biological hallucinations (\u00a73.6-3.8). Figure 1 provides a system overview.\nRVQ-Alpha: Bridging Single-Cell Transcriptomics and Large Language Models via Discrete Tokenization and Verifiable Reinforcement Learning",
./data/living_catalog/taxonomy_rerun_preflight_2026-08-12/taxonomy/runs/classification_dense/shard_04/records/june_update_2026-06-10__rec_000121_8f4709456aba/june_update_2026_06_10_rec_000121_8f4709456aba_docling_json_20260812_214234/debug/dense_provenance.json:2802:        "3.3 scCoT-Synth: Evidence-Grounded Supervision Engine for Cold-Start RVQ Alignment"
./data/living_catalog/taxonomy_rerun_preflight_2026-08-12/taxonomy/runs/classification_dense/shard_04/records/june_update_2026-06-10__rec_000121_8f4709456aba/june_update_2026_06_10_rec_000121_8f4709456aba_docling_json_20260812_214234/debug/dense_provenance.json:2807:      "text": "3 Method\n3.3 scCoT-Synth: Evidence-Grounded Supervision Engine for Cold-Start RVQ Alignment\nThe 256 RVQ tokens introduced during vocabulary expansion carry no pretrained semantics. This cold-start grounding problem compounds the reasoning-format challenge of DeepSeek-R1 [32] with a cross-modal dimension.\nscCoT-Synth addresses this issue by requiring every CoT training trajectory to decode RVQ codes into verifiable gene evidence before reasoning. Consequently, the standard next-token prediction loss forces the RVQ embeddings toward the gene-name representations already encoded in the pretrained weights.\nThe resulting engine produces approximately 600K training samples covering 46 task variants that span the seven task families.\nEvidence-first constraint. Every CoT training sample follows a directed evidence-reasoning chain:\navailable under a CC-BY-NC-ND 4.0 International license. (which was not certified by peer review) is the author/funder, who has granted bioRxiv a license to display the preprint in perpetuity. It is made bioRxiv preprint doi: https://doi.org/10.64898/2026.04.20.719773; this version posted April 23, 2026. The copyright holder for this preprint\nRVQ-Alpha: Bridging Single-Cell Transcriptomics and Large Language Models via Discrete Tokenization and Verifiable Reinforcement Learning\n<!-- formula-not-decoded -->\nwhere c = ( c 0, . . . , c 7 ) denotes the RVQ codes and t denotes the task instruction.\nThe model must produce verifiable gene evidence E (e.g., 'elevated CD8A , CD8B , GZMB ; absent CD4 ') before any reasoning step R .\nBecause gene-name tokens in E are predicted from RVQ input positions via the attention mechanism, the cross-entropy loss on these tokens provides a dense supervisory signal that pulls RVQ embeddings toward the pretrained gene-name representations, without requiring any explicit alignment module.\nScaffolded teacher-student synthesis. The constraint is realized through a teacher-student protocol with asymmetric information.\nDuring teacher synthesis , a replaceable LLM backend receives curated gene features (such as expressionranked genes, known markers, active transcription factors, and functional gene modules) alongside c and t , enabling biologically accurate evidence-first reasoning.\nA conclusion-blind elicitation protocol prevents the teacher from short-circuiting this process. Although the teacher receives metadata labels for context anchoring, the system prompt constrains it to derive conclusions solely from gene evidence, reasoning as if discovering them for the first time. Deterministic validators flag outputs that reference labels directly. For continued-pretraining data, the teacher regenerates these flagged samples; for CoT data, the flag is recorded as a non-blocking quality signal.\nDuring student training , gene features are stripped entirely, and the input to the student contains only c \u2295 t .\nGene names survive solely in the assistant response (the training target) as evidence claims that the student must learn to predict from the RVQ codes alone.\nThe gene features thus act as scaffolding : they are present during construction to ensure teacher accuracy and absent during training to force genuine RVQ grounding.\nTask-grounded generation at scale. Grounding RVQ tokens requires exposure across various biological granularities, including individual cell profiles, cell populations, and extended expository contexts, because a single granularity would bias the learned representations toward that specific level of description.",
./data/living_catalog/taxonomy_rerun_preflight_2026-08-12/taxonomy/runs/classification_dense/shard_04/records/june_update_2026-06-10__rec_000121_8f4709456aba/june_update_2026_06_10_rec_000121_8f4709456aba_docling_json_20260812_214234/debug/dense_provenance.json:3070:        "3.3 scCoT-Synth: Evidence-Grounded Supervision Engine for Cold-Start RVQ Alignment"
./data/living_catalog/taxonomy_rerun_preflight_2026-08-12/taxonomy/runs/classification_dense/shard_04/records/june_update_2026-06-10__rec_000121_8f4709456aba/june_update_2026_06_10_rec_000121_8f4709456aba_docling_json_20260812_214234/debug/dense_provenance.json:3075:      "text": "3 Method\n3.3 scCoT-Synth: Evidence-Grounded Supervision Engine for Cold-Start RVQ Alignment\nscCoT-Synth therefore comprises three generation tiers: (i) cell-level CoT generation across five annotation tasks (cell-type classification, tissue classification, disease classification, gene-name reconstruction, and expression-profile generation); (ii) population-level CoT across five tasks operating on groups of up to \u223c 50 cells; and (iii) audience-diversified continued pretraining drawn from a combinatorial space defined by four audience profiles, nine stylistic templates, and up to 108 variants along four content dimensions (analysis depth, reasoning path, gene organization, and data format).\nAll tiers share the core design principles of teacher scaffolding and conclusion-blind elicitation, adapted to the output format of each tier.\nMulti-layer verification. Every generated trajectory passes through a verification stack spanning deterministic structural checks, rubric-based semantic scoring, and RVQ arithmetic validation (Table 2).\nRVQ-Alpha: Bridging Single-Cell Transcriptomics and Large Language Models via Discrete Tokenization and Verifiable Reinforcement Learning\nTable 2: Verification stack. Layers 1-5 are enforced during data construction; Layers 6-7 apply across all pipelines. \u2020 Non-blocking quality signal recorded with the CoT sample but never used to discard it. \u2021 Blocking criterion for continued-pretraining samples; failures are regenerated by the teacher.\n\n1, Name = Context constraint. 1, Method = System-prompt behavioral rule. 1, Enforcement = Soft \u2020. 2, Name = Evidence-first structure. 2, Method = Regex position check. 2, Enforcement = Soft \u2020 / Hard \u2021. 3, Name = Forbidden reference. 3, Method = Phrase filter. 3, Enforcement = Soft \u2020 / Hard \u2021. 4, Name = Reasoning-conclusion. 4, Method = Regex label extraction. 4, Enforcement = Soft \u2020. 5, Name = LLM-as-judge rubric. 5, Method = Weighted multi-dim rubric. 5, Enforcement = Soft (scored). 6, Name = RVQ code arithmetic. 6, Method = Offset + range validation. 6, Enforcement = Blocking criterion. 7, Name = Nomenclature norm.. 7, Method = Curated mapping rules. 7, Enforcement = Blocking criterion\nThe LLM-as-judge (Layer 5) evaluates CoT samples across four dimensions (evidence grounding, logic rigor, factual accuracy, and uncertainty calibration), utilizing a separate five-dimensional profile for continued-pretraining data. 2\nThis verification stack yields the final corpus of approximately 600K quality-assessed SFT samples across the 46 task variants.\nWhy it works: gradient pathway for cross-modal alignment. The evidence-first structure creates a gradient pathway from gene-name prediction positions back to RVQ embeddings via the attention value path:\n<!-- formula-not-decoded -->\nwhere AE indexes gene-evidence token positions and \u03b1 i , j is the attention weight from position i to RVQ position j .\nWithin each layer, the gradient on e RVQ j is modulated by the attention mass assigned to that code at gene-prediction positions. This mechanism represents one of several gradient pathways that together provide a cross-modal supervisory signal without requiring an explicit mapping layer.\nAblation studies confirm this effect: removing evidence-first generation degrades accuracy by 8.3,pp and increases hallucinations from 4.2% to 23.7% (\u00a76).",
./data/living_catalog/taxonomy_rerun_preflight_2026-08-12/taxonomy/runs/classification_dense/shard_04/records/june_update_2026-06-10__rec_000121_8f4709456aba/june_update_2026_06_10_rec_000121_8f4709456aba_docling_json_20260812_214234/debug/dense_provenance.json:3128:        "3.3 scCoT-Synth: Evidence-Grounded Supervision Engine for Cold-Start RVQ Alignment"
./data/living_catalog/taxonomy_rerun_preflight_2026-08-12/taxonomy/runs/classification_dense/shard_04/records/june_update_2026-06-10__rec_000121_8f4709456aba/june_update_2026_06_10_rec_000121_8f4709456aba_docling_json_20260812_214234/debug/dense_provenance.json:3133:      "text": "3 Method\n3.3 scCoT-Synth: Evidence-Grounded Supervision Engine for Cold-Start RVQ Alignment\nThe resulting corpus of evidence-grounded trajectories (comprising CoT chains and augmented narratives) provides the initial SFT supervision for cold-start RVQ alignment.\nThe structured output format, where gene evidence E precedes reasoning R , enables the downstream Fact-Aware RLVR module (\u00a73.8) to decompose predictions into atomic biological claims for expressiongrounded reward verification.",
./data/living_catalog/taxonomy_rerun_preflight_2026-08-12/taxonomy/runs/classification_dense/shard_04/records/june_update_2026-06-10__rec_000121_8f4709456aba/june_update_2026_06_10_rec_000121_8f4709456aba_docling_json_20260812_214234/debug/dense_provenance.json:3710:      "text": "3 Method\n3.4 Multi-Stage Training Pipeline\nStage 2: Multi-Task SFT\nThe goal of Stage 2 is to teach the model structured instruction following and chain-of-thought reasoning across seven single-cell task families.\nThe Stage 1 checkpoint is fine-tuned on the full scCoT-Synth corpus. Each training example carries a task-family annotation that selects the appropriate input formatting and loss masking for one of the seven task families.\nStage 2 performs full fine-tuning of the language-model backbone while keeping the upstream RVQ encoder frozen.\nThe loss is restricted to assistant token positions, ensuring that the model learns to generate responses rather than memorize prompts:\navailable under a CC-BY-NC-ND 4.0 International license. (which was not certified by peer review) is the author/funder, who has granted bioRxiv a license to display the preprint in perpetuity. It is made bioRxiv preprint doi: https://doi.org/10.64898/2026.04.20.719773; this version posted April 23, 2026. The copyright holder for this preprint\nRVQ-Alpha: Bridging Single-Cell Transcriptomics and Large Language Models via Discrete Tokenization and Verifiable Reinforcement Learning\n<!-- formula-not-decoded -->\nwhere A indexes assistant tokens, t denotes the task instruction, and f enc ( x ) represents the RVQ cell encoding.\nDuring training, sampling weights across task families are adjusted to prevent any single dataset from dominating the gradient signal.\nHowever, the output quality of the model remains bounded by the training distribution, which motivates the reward-driven optimization of Stage 3.",
